  "findings": [
    "The six reviewed R46/R47 named source standard clauses and selected numeric fields match between official 2024 Version 2 and 2025 Version 3 PDF page views; this is NOT proof that all pages/footnotes/amendments of Chapter 2.3 are unchanged.",
    "The Murabba definition permits fruit, rhizome or vegetable sources but prints fruit-content >=55%; nonfruit variant legal interpretation is still evidence-held.",
    "Fruit Cheese's 25% strawberry/raspberry exception cannot be borrowed by other fruit variants.",
    "Frozen Vegetables has required negative peroxidase, but this may not be transferred to separately standardized Frozen Fruit 2.3.37.",
    "Coconut milk and cream source standards allow sodium caseinate; 'non-dairy' names do not automatically mean milk-allergen-free or vegan and need actual SKU formula/claim review.",
    "The stray right bracket in the Coconut Milk Powder bulk density source cell '0.3–0.45]' appears in both 2024 and 2025 compendia; it is unresolved editorial typography, not a newly introduced or removed legal limit.",
    "Full current original Gazette notifications, product-specific contaminant article selection, every applicable amendment, analytical sampling and actual SKU/laboratory data remain missing.",
    "This is source edition validation only; does not change R46 or R47 original audit evidentiary statements, numerical rules, deployed helper, or original source product master."
  ],
